<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">NGO Accounting in Delhi: FCRA, 12A/80G, and Fund Compliance</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - NGO & Non-Profit Accounting in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>NGO accounting = fund-based accounting + FCRA (SBI Sansad Marg designated account, FC-4 by 31 Dec, 20% admin cap) + 12A/80G (5-year renewal, S.11 85% application) + CSR-1 + donor reporting. Delhi = 13,763 NGOs (3rd highest in India). MHA FCRA Section + SBI Sansad Marg + IT offices all in Delhi. From Rs 8,000/month. Patron Rohini office.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi is the nerve centre of India's non-profit sector. For a comprehensive overview, see our <a href="/ngo-and-non-profit-accounting-services">NGO Accounting</a> national guide.</p><div class="table-responsive-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Governing Acts</td><td>Societies Act 1860, Trusts Act 1882, Companies Act (S.8), IT Act (S.11/12A/80G), FCRA 2010, CSR Rules</td></tr><tr><td>Cost From</td><td>Rs 8,000/month (small NGO); Rs 15,000 (FCRA-registered)</td></tr><tr><td>Key Portals</td><td>incometax.gov.in, fcraonline.nic.in, ngodarpan.gov.in, csr.gov.in</td></tr><tr><td>Penalty</td><td>Loss of 12A = entire income taxable. FCRA cancellation. Max marginal rate</td></tr><tr><td>Delhi Context</td><td>13,763 NGOs. MHA FCRA Section in Delhi. SBI Sansad Marg mandatory. IT offices at ITO</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p</p>
                <p>Goonj, CARE India, Smile Foundation, CRY, World Vision, Oxfam India headquartered here. UN agencies and bilateral donors in Lodhi Estate/Chanakyapuri. FCRA Amendment 2020: mandatory SBI Sansad Marg account. 12A/80G now 5-year renewal. Patron's Rohini office handles MHA, IT, Registrar of Societies filings.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is NGO and Non-Profit Accounting?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>Definition:</strong> Specialised financial management where income must be applied exclusively for charitable objects, fund receipts tracked by source/purpose, and compliance under IT Act (S.11/12A/80G), FCRA 2010, and applicable registration act determines tax-exempt status.</p><p><strong>Delhi context:</strong> Proximity to central regulators means faster scrutiny. Form 10B if income >Rs 5Cr. Form 10BD by 31 May. Surplus ≤15% (S.11(1)(a)). FCRA: FC-4 by 31 Dec, SBI Sansad Marg, admin ≤20%.</p><p><strong>Key terms:</strong> Fund Accounting (segregated general/restricted/corpus/project funds), FCRA (foreign contribution), 12A (tax exemption), 80G (donor deduction), CSR-1 (corporate CSR eligibility).</p><p>See <a href="/accounting-services">Accounting Services</a> for general business accounting.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for NGO & Non-Profit Accounting in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>12A:</strong> Tax exemption registration. 5-year renewal since 2020 amendment. Income applied to charitable purposes. Form 10B audit report.</p><p><strong>FCRA:</strong> Foreign Contribution Regulation Act. SBI Sansad Marg designated account. FC-4 by 31 Dec. Admin ≤20%. 5-year validity.</p><p><strong>Fund Accounting:</strong> General fund, restricted fund, corpus fund, project-specific. Separate income/expenditure/balance per fund.</p><p><strong>CSR-1:</strong> MCA portal registration for receiving corporate CSR funds. Linked to PAN + 12A/80G. Unique CSR Registration Number.</p><p><strong>Form FC-4:</strong> FCRA annual return. All foreign contributions received, utilised, balance. Due 31 December. Non-filing = cancellation risk.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
